JJ DAI Reference Implementation — Licensing
===========================================

This repository is licensed under a two-license structure:

1. AGPL-3.0-only — the trust/governance CORE:
   jjdai/, core/, kernel/, node/, m1m5/, tests/, scripts/
   Full text: LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt
   Rationale: JJ DAI nodes provide inference, verification and witness
   services to other nodes and their stewards OVER A NETWORK. The AGPL
   §13 network-interaction clause obliges operators of modified nodes
   to make their modified source available to the users who interact
   with them — aligning the license with the network's core property:
   verifiability. Opaque production forks are contrary to both.

2. Apache-2.0 — the NECS specification and conformance harness:
   necs/
   Full text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
   Rationale: NECS is a SPECIFICATION. Third-party engine vendors must
   be able to implement and certify against it without copyleft
   obligations, maximizing the diversity of independent verifiers —
   which the network's security model depends on.

Unless a file states otherwise, the license of its top-level directory
applies. SPDX identifiers: AGPL-3.0-only, Apache-2.0.

Copyright (c) 2026 JJ GROUP / JJ DAI contributors.
